 "intro": "On the river Sucro (Júcar) in eastern Spain, 75 BC. You are Pompey, thirty years old, sent against the rebel Roman general Sertorius. Your colleague Metellus Pius is on his way.",
 "debrief": "In Plutarch’s account, Pompey attacked before Metellus arrived, wanting the glory. Sertorius beat Pompey’s wing; Pompey was wounded and escaped because the enemy fought over his richly decorated horse. On the other wing Afranius broke into Sertorius’s camp, but his men stopped to loot and were cut down. Metellus arrived next morning. Sertorius is said to have joked that if 'the old woman' had not come he would have whipped 'the boy' back to Rome. The other choices are what-ifs.",
